ee66f0b009bf63d27081c8ff14fe65dbaf409b8b6bf2b39f8127b162059c7acb{"version":1,"source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"},"layers":{"businessProfile":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"25b5c989eef12184e9283b2198ca52f4443bb08d1857c42dc0f31a6ab983798b","quote":"We are a leading provider of Technology Management as a Service (TMaaS) that consists of federally certified communications management, identity management, and interactive bill presentment and unified communication analytics solutions and IT as a Service (ITaaS). We help our clients achieve their organizational missions for mobility management and security objectives in this challenging and complex business environment.","context":"Business Overview","section":"Business Overview","block":264,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"e9902e906da2d6cbf44fb213483f71f967d0fb11ad090c89492798522e92c79c","quote":"We offer our TMaaS solutions through a flexible “As-a-Service” model or “Xaas” which includes both a scalable and comprehensive set of functional capabilities that can be used by any customer to meet the most common functional, technical and security requirements for mobility management. Our TMaaS solutions were designed and implemented with flexibility in mind such that it can accommodate a large variety of customer requirements through simple configuration settings rather than through costly software development. The flexibility of our TMaaS solutions enables our customers to be able to quickly expand or contract their mobility management requirements. Our TMaaS solutions are hosted and accessible on-demand through a secure federal government certified proprietary portal that provides our customers with the ability to manage, analyze and protect their valuable communications assets, and deploy identity management solutions that provide secured virtual and physical access to restricted environments.","context":"We are a leading provider of Technology Management as a Service (TMaaS) that consists of federally certified communications management, identity management, and interactive bill presentment and unified communication analytics solutions and IT as a Service (ITaaS). We help our clients achieve their organizational missions for mobility management and security objectives in this challenging and complex business environment.","section":"Business Overview","block":265,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"e1aaf635be3bdf1db441cdad564834a59e7e7bbbffb300e3700e9618605eea1a","quote":"For additional information related to our business operations, see the description of our business set forth in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2025 filed with the SEC on March 25, 2026.","context":"We offer our TMaaS solutions through a flexible “As-a-Service” model or “Xaas” which includes both a scalable and comprehensive set of functional capabilities that can be used by any customer to meet the most common functional, technical and security requirements for mobility management. Our TMaaS solutions were designed and implemented with flexibility in mind such that it can accommodate a large variety of customer requirements through simple configuration settings rather than through costly software development. The flexibility of our TMaaS solutions enables our customers to be able to quickly expand or contract their mobility management requirements. Our TMaaS solutions are hosted and accessible on-demand through a secure federal government certified proprietary portal that provides our customers with the ability to manage, analyze and protect their valuable communications assets, and deploy identity management solutions that provide secured virtual and physical access to restricted environments.","section":"Business Overview","block":266,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"9835067919c39ea6b41c49c1023bd427615703848bbeeb2f1e23b368241a028a","quote":"On June 24, 2026, we were selected as the single awardee of the Department of Homeland Security's (DHS) Cellular Wireless Managed Services (CWMS) 3.0 contract, a 10-year Indefinite Delivery, Indefinite Quantity (IDIQ) contract consisting of a one-year base period and nine one-year option periods with a contract ceiling value of approximately $3.1 billion. Under the CWMS 3.0 award, we will deliver and manage an integrated portfolio of solutions that support lifecycle management, connectivity, security, and operational requirements across all DHS components. Although the Company has been selected for the contract, on June 29, 2026, we were notified that a post-award protest was filed with respect to the contract.","context":"Second Quarter Highlights","section":"Business Overview","block":270,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"6e6ec03b599d0a47e01d4bf219467c3ffb44ff30db3c787b2c27187a2400fe0c","quote":"Our longer-term strategic focus and goals are driven by our need to expand our critical mass so that we have more flexibility to fund investments in technology solutions and introduce new sales and marketing initiatives in order to expand our marketplace share and increase the breadth of our offerings in order to improve company sustainability and growth.","context":"Strategic Focus","section":"Business Overview","block":272,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"acb684a47cd9222d3865250e238f1f97dc3948fc4c78c539fbc12ab9fe53a722","quote":"In fiscal 2026, we wi