3.0 award. These arrangements include up to approximately $0.6 million of cash incentive compensation expected to be paid upon satisfaction of the applicable performance condition, as well as up to approximately $0.4 million of stock-based compensation that would be recognized over the applicable requisite service periods following satisfaction of the performance condition. The timing, amount and financial statement impact of these costs will depend on the outcome and timing of the protest process, the final terms of the award, employee service requirements, forfeitures, and other factors. Accordingly, there can be no assurance as to the timing or amount of any future compensation expense.","context":"We expect to incur additional costs in future periods related to our move from a smaller reporting company to an accelerated filer, including increased external audit fees, consulting services, additional personnel and other compliance-related expenditures. Based on current estimates, these incremental costs are expected to approximate $0.8 million during the second half of 2026.","section":"Results of Operations","block":294,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"c5aac18c4cd555f81468a14c8796bacaf1793967fa10dacd75a5d316c1f234bc","quote":"Depreciation and Amortization. Depreciation and amortization expense for the three months ended June 30, 2026 was $181,400 which is consistent as compared to $233,100 in 2025.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Results of Operations","block":297,"table":null,"attribution":"management","i