th in the number of phone lines under management during the second half of 2025 for our DHS customer.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Results of Operations","block":308,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"6bac289e6faf7ab2fed112dfbc71a520a8cff43210c9f19872cb08900823f670","quote":"Cost of Revenues. Our cost of revenues include employee labor, excluding fringe benefit costs, and subcontractors directly associated with satisfying customer performance obligations, cash back rewards received associated with vendor payments made on behalf of customers, and the associated cost of products and third-party software that we resell to our end customers. Cost of revenues also includes depreciation and amortization of capitalized software related to delivering our solutions. Cost of revenues for the six months ended June 30, 2026 were $67.1 million (or 85% of revenues) and was consistent cost of revenues in the same period in 2025. Included in cost of revenues is carrier costs paid on behalf of our federal government customers of approximately $48.4 million and $43.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively.","context":"Carrier Service Revenues. Our carrier services revenue was $49.8 million, an increase of $5.2 million, as compared with the same period in 2025. The increase in carrier services revenues over the same period last year is a result of the growth in the number of phone lines under management during the second half of 2025 for our DHS customer.","section":"Results of Operations","block":309,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1034760/000165495426007588/wyy_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6.bin","sha256":"c4e26c824ece9bf274d7199d10d435459a9b41dd1831288711ddb6aa29562db6"}},{"id":"5887a70677d78c88088f9fe7bc937feecbd08123c52842a0eebd57e398388889","quote":"Gross Profit. Gross profit for the six month period ended June 30, 2026 increased on a dollar basis by $1.5 million to $11.4 million (or 15% of revenues), compared to $9.9 million (or 14% of revenues) in the same period in 2025.","context":"Cost of Revenues. Our cost of revenues include employee labor, excluding fringe benefit costs, and subcontractors directly associated with satisfying customer performance obligations, cash back rewards received associated with vendor payments made on behalf of customers, and the associated cost of products and third-party software that we resell to our end customers. Cost of revenues also includes depreciation and amortization of capitalized software related to delivering our solutions. Cost of revenues for the six months ended June 30, 2026 were $67.1 million (or 85% of revenues) and was consistent cost of revenues in the same period in 2025. Included in cost of revenues is carrier costs paid on behalf of our federal government customers of approximately $48.4 million and $43.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively.","section":"Results of Operations","block":310,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-007588","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001034760","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/103476